.SH NAME
ns_perm \- Add users, groups, and permissions
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBns_perm adduser\fR ?\fB-allow\fR? ?\fB-deny\fR? ?\fB-clear\fR? ?\fB-salt \fIvalue\fR\fR? ?--? \fIname\fR \fIencpass\fR \fIuserfield\fR ?\fIhost \&.\&.\&.\fR?
.sp
\fBns_perm deluser\fR \fIname\fR
.sp
\fBns_perm addgroup\fR \fIgroup\fR \fIuser\fR ?\fIuser \&.\&.\&.\fR?
.sp
\fBns_perm delgroup\fR \fIname\fR
.sp
\fBns_perm allowuser\fR ?\fB-noinherit\fR? ?--? \fImethod\fR \fIurl\fR \fIuser \&.\&.\&.\fR
.sp
\fBns_perm denyuser\fR ?\fB-noinherit\fR? ?--? \fImethod\fR \fIurl\fR \fIuser \&.\&.\&.\fR
.sp
\fBns_perm allowgroup\fR ?\fB-noinherit\fR? ?--? \fImethod\fR \fIurl\fR \fIgroup \&.\&.\&.\fR
.sp
\fBns_perm denygroup\fR ?\fB-noinherit\fR? ?--? \fImethod\fR \fIurl\fR \fIgroup \&.\&.\&.\fR
.sp
\fBns_perm checkpass\fR \fIuser\fR \fIpasswd\fR
.sp
\fBns_perm setpass\fR \fIuser\fR \fIencpass\fR ?\fIsalt\fR?
.sp
\fBns_perm listusers\fR
.sp
\fBns_perm listgroups\fR
.sp
\fBns_perm listperms\fR
.sp
\fBns_permreload\fR
.sp
\fBns_permpasswd\fR \fIuser\fR \fIoldpasswd\fR \fInewpasswd\fR
.sp
.BE
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBns_perm\fR implements a command set for simple password and group
management for NaviServer\&.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBns_perm adduser\fR ?\fB-allow\fR? ?\fB-deny\fR? ?\fB-clear\fR? ?\fB-salt \fIvalue\fR\fR? ?--? \fIname\fR \fIencpass\fR \fIuserfield\fR ?\fIhost \&.\&.\&.\fR?
Adds a new user to the in-memory users database\&. When a
\fBpasswd\fR file is given, this command is used to load the users
from this file\&.
The user is
identified by the specified \fIname\fR, and the provided encrypted
password \fIencpass\fR and additional user information
(\fIuserfield\fR) are stored in the database\&.
.sp
If the \fB-allow\fR option is used along with one or more
hostnames, the user is granted access only on the specified hosts\&.
.sp
If the \fB-deny\fR option is used along with hostnames,
access for the user is explicitly denied on those hosts\&. Hostnames can
be specified as an IP address with netmask (e\&.g\&.,
\fB128\&.2\&.142\&.0/255\&.255\&.255\&.0\fR),
a fully qualified domain name (e\&.g\&., \fBwww\&.microsoft\&.com\fR),
or as a domain pattern (e\&.g\&., \fB\&.microsoft\&.com\fR)\&.
.CS


 128\&.2\&.142\&.0/255\&.255\&.255\&.0 or www\&.microsoft\&.com or \&.microsoft\&.com\&.

.CE
.sp
\fB-salt\fR
By default, the password provided in \fIencpass\fR is assumed to be
already encrypted with the \fBns_crypt\fR command using the salt
\fBCU\fR\&. When the \fB-salt\fR is specified, the \fIencpass\fR argument
is treated as clear text and will be encrypted using the specified
salt via \fBns_crypt\fR\&.
.CS


 ns_crypt mypasswd CU

.CE
.sp
The \fB-clear\fR indicates that the password should be stored in
clear text rather than encrypted\&.
.TP
\fBns_perm deluser\fR \fIname\fR
Removes the user with the given \fIname\fR from the users database\&.
.TP
\fBns_perm addgroup\fR \fIgroup\fR \fIuser\fR ?\fIuser \&.\&.\&.\fR?
Creates a new group identified by \fIgroup\fR and adds the specified
user(s) (\fIuser\fR and any additional users) to that group\&.
.TP
\fBns_perm delgroup\fR \fIname\fR
Deletes the group identified by \fIname\fR from the system\&.
.TP
\fBns_perm allowuser\fR ?\fB-noinherit\fR? ?--? \fImethod\fR \fIurl\fR \fIuser \&.\&.\&.\fR
Allows the specified user(s) to access the combination of the HTTP
\fImethod\fR and \fIurl\fR\&. If \fB-noinherit\fR is specified, only
the exact URL is matched; otherwise, all URLs under the given URL are
permitted\&.
.TP
\fBns_perm denyuser\fR ?\fB-noinherit\fR? ?--? \fImethod\fR \fIurl\fR \fIuser \&.\&.\&.\fR
Denies access for the specified user(s) to the given HTTP \fImethod\fR
and \fIurl\fR\&. With \fB-noinherit\fR, the restriction applies only
to the exact URL; without it, all URLs beneath the given URL are
denied\&.
.TP
\fBns_perm allowgroup\fR ?\fB-noinherit\fR? ?--? \fImethod\fR \fIurl\fR \fIgroup \&.\&.\&.\fR
Grants access for the specified group(s) to the HTTP \fImethod\fR and
\fIurl\fR\&. The \fB-noinherit\fR behaves as described above\&.
.TP
\fBns_perm denygroup\fR ?\fB-noinherit\fR? ?--? \fImethod\fR \fIurl\fR \fIgroup \&.\&.\&.\fR
Denies access for the specified group(s) to the HTTP \fImethod\fR and
\fIurl\fR\&. When \fB-noinherit\fR is used, only the exact URL is
affected; otherwise, the rule applies recursively to subordinate URLs\&.
.TP
\fBns_perm checkpass\fR \fIuser\fR \fIpasswd\fR
Verifies that the given plain-text \fIpasswd\fR is correct for the
user specified by \fIuser\fR\&. If the password does not match, a Tcl
error is thrown\&.
.TP
\fBns_perm setpass\fR \fIuser\fR \fIencpass\fR ?\fIsalt\fR?
Updates the password for the user specified by \fIuser\fR to the new
encrypted password \fIencpass\fR\&. If a \fIsalt\fR is provided, the
password is expected to be in clear text and will be encrypted using
\fBns_crypt\fR with the given salt\&.
.TP
\fBns_perm listusers\fR
Returns a Tcl list of all users in the system\&. For each user, the list
includes three elements: the username, the encrypted password, and the
user's permissions\&.
.TP
\fBns_perm listgroups\fR
Returns a Tcl list of all registered groups\&. Each group is represented
by its group name followed by a list of its members\&.
.TP
\fBns_perm listperms\fR
Returns a Tcl list of all allow/deny rules registered for each URL\&.
.TP
\fBns_permreload\fR
Reloads all nsperm files\&. Note that on very busy sites this operation
may cause temporary authentication failures, as the in-memory
permissions are cleared before the files are reloaded from disk\&.
.TP
\fBns_permpasswd\fR \fIuser\fR \fIoldpasswd\fR \fInewpasswd\fR
Updates the password for an existing user both in the running server’s
memory and in the persistent \fBpasswd\fR file on disk\&. The \fIuser\fR
parameter specifies the username whose password is to be updated\&. The
\fIoldpasswd\fR parameter must be provided in plain text and
represents either the user's current password or the nsadmin
password\&. The \fInewpasswd\fR parameter is the new password, also
supplied in plain text\&.
.PP
.SH CONFIGURATION
The following configuration options are available to control
permission module:
.TP
htaccess
This parameter if set to true, enables \&.htaccess mode, similar to what
the Apache web server has but very simple and limited in
functionality\&.
.sp
On every request the server looks for \&.htaccess file in the
current request directory and loads it if modified since the last
read\&. The structure of the file is simple:
.CS


 allow user \&.\&.\&.
 deny user \&.\&.\&.

.CE
.TP
passwdfile
This parameter determines in \&.htaccess mode which file with users and
passwords needs to be checked for modification and reloaded
automatically\&. If \&.htaccess mode is not active, the parameter is
ignored\&.
.PP
.CS


 ns_section ns/server/$server/module/nsperm {
   ns_param htaccess   true
   ns_param passwdfile /usr/local/ns/modules/nsperm/passwd
 }

.CE
.SH EXAMPLES
.CS


 ns_perm adduser test [ns_crypt testpass ""] TestUser
 ns_perm adduser -salt CU test2 test TestUser2

 ns_perm allowuser GET /Documents test test2

.CE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
ns_crypt, nsd
.SH KEYWORDS
NaviServer, nsperm, server built-in
